# A negative literal needs no parentheses to be an argument: `math/round -3.5`
# passes minus three and a half (ruled 2026-09-30), so the parentheses in
# `math/round (-3.5)` group nothing. Before the ruling this refusal said the
# same thing and was false, since `math/round -3.5` parsed as a subtraction.
import "std/math"

main = print "{math/round (-3.5)}"
